# Docker build-context exclusions for the AgentCore Runtime image asset.
#
# The Runtime image asset (infra-cdk/mahalo_infra/runtime_stack.py, the
# `AgentRuntimeArtifact.from_asset(_REPO_ROOT, file="agent/Dockerfile", …)`
# deploy branch) uses THIS repo root as the Docker build context. The Docker
# daemon honors this file when it tars the context, independent of the CDK-level
# `exclude=` in runtime_stack.py — belt-and-suspenders for the same bug.
#
# Root cause these entries prevent: the context root contains infra-cdk/cdk.out,
# the CDK output dir that itself holds staged assets. Copying it into a new asset
# nests cdk.out recursively (cdk.out/asset.<h>/infra-cdk/cdk.out/asset.<h>/…) and
# fails staging with ENAMETOOLONG. The dev virtualenvs (agent/.venv, api/.venv)
# are excluded too: the image installs deps via `pip install -r agent/requirements.txt`
# (agent/Dockerfile), so the committed local venvs are never needed and only bloat.
#
# Do NOT add agent/ or agent/requirements.txt here — the image COPYs them.

# CDK output (the recursion source)
infra-cdk/cdk.out
**/cdk.out

# Local dev virtualenvs (not needed; deps come from pip + requirements.txt)
.venv
**/.venv

# Python caches
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
.pytest_cache
**/.pytest_cache

# VCS metadata
.git

# Node / frontend build artifacts (not part of the agent image)
**/node_modules
frontend/out
frontend/.next
